Author: Peter Svensson <psvensson@gmail.com>
Date:   Sun Jul 5 23:20:04 2026 +0200

    fix(rebalancer): credit a drain-phase REPLACE's replacement in deficit accounting
    
    The single in-flight-aware replica accounting computed
    deficitEffectiveCount = activeCount + inFlightAddCount, deliberately excluding a
    REPLACE's replacement ("a REPLACE is net-neutral, never fills a deficit"). That
    holds while the REPLACE's source is still an active voter — but once the source
    has DRAINED (left activeCount) while the replacement is still a durable non-voting
    LEARNER (a materialized syncing row, not yet ACTIVE), the replacement's slot is
    counted NOWHERE. The move planner then reads a false deficit (e.g. 2-of-3), mints
    a spurious count-increasing ADD, the learner promotes -> 4 voters over a target of
    3, the group concentrates, and the over-target ADD is deferred forever with no
    count-neutral REPLACE pairing -> the partition never de-concentrates.
    
    Live: this is what stalled cold 5-node formation of the service-data-affinity
    demo (run-4: replica_operations-p1 stuck 4-voters/2-on-seed the whole window ->
    quorum_concentrated -> the ledger self-move interlock held all other ops ->
    control plane never settled -> [2/4] load timed out).
    
    Fix (industry pattern: TiKV/PD "projected = current + in-flight operator
    influence"; CockroachDB counts the learner in atomic replication changes): credit
    toward deficitEffectiveCount the SPECIFIC replacement row of each drain-phase
    REPLACE — the non-active occupied replica on the op's target node — ROW-OP-LINKED,
    excluding replacements already ACTIVE, stale learners unlinked to a REPLACE, and
    net-neutral (source-still-active) REPLACEs. This is a read-path correctness fix,
    not a count heuristic, which is why it bounds where 3 prior count-based
    approximations were refuted.
    
    Proven against the four recorded constraint tuples
    (active/occupied/inFlightAdd/drainPhaseReplace): stale-syncing 1/3/0/0->ADD,
    serialization 2/2/0/1->ADD, run-28 2/3/0/1->suppress, verifier-starvation
    1/3/0/1->ADD, plus a net-neutral guard. DT
    test/rebalancer/in-flight-aware-drain-phase-replace-credit.test.js; dt:prove
    red-on-revert PROVEN; regression 616/616 across the accounting-consumer +
    move-planner/replace suites; lint + complexity clean.
    
    Live effect (demo run-5): replica_operations-p1 over-target deferrals 148->4 (the
    ledger de-concentrates), formation completions 23->54, no 120s hard stall. Full
    cold-formation quiescence not yet reached (the other system partitions still
    spread via glacially-completing serialized REPLACEs) — that residual is the next
    step; this removes the ledger's over-target deadlock.
    
    Research: solve/changes/formation-ledger-over-target-accounting-drain-phase-replace-blind-spot/industry-rebalance-patterns.md
    
